    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1564">

                <pb facs="1161" n="1045" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1045"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/676.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Bonney to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San Luis Potosi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please to request General Carranza, Vera Cruz, to instruct his General M. Zapata
                    in Tula, Tamaulipas, to respect all property there belonging to Spanish Vice
                    Consul of San Luis Potosí consisting of hides, ixtle and plantation, now
                    threatened by that General.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bonney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
